<title>RUSSIA: Russia Jan-Nov sugar imports down, cocoa/coffee up.</title>
<headline>Russia Jan-Nov sugar imports down, cocoa/coffee up.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia imported 1.38 million tonnes of refined sugar from all countries in the first 11 months of 1996, down 12 percent from year-ago levels, data from the State Statistics Committee showed on Friday.</p>
<p>The data, as reported by Interfax news agency, showed refined sugar imports from countries outside the Commonwealth of Independent States slumped 57 percent year-on-year to 143,000 tonnes in January to November last year.</p>
<p>Non-CIS imports of raw sugar shot up 56 percent to 1.61 million tonnes in January-November 1996, the committee said.</p>
<p>Non-CIS imports of cocoa edged higher to 47,700 tonnes in the first 11 months of 1996 from 47,000 over the same 1995 period, and non-CIS coffee imports rose to 23,700 tonnes from 23,300 tonnes, committee figures showed.</p>
<p>The committee released the following data for soft commodity imports --</p>
<p>	    RUSSIAN IMPORTS OF SUGAR, COFFEE AND COCOA</p>
<p>			Jan-Nov 1996     Jan-Nov 1995    pct change</p>
<p>			  (tonnes)	   (tonnes)	  yr/yr</p>
<p>(CIS and non-CIS)</p>
<p> Refined sugar     1,384,600	  1,581,500	   -12</p>
<p>(Non-CIS)</p>
<p> Refined sugar	 143,000	    329,200	   -57</p>
<p> Raw sugar	   1,614,300	  1,035,800	   +56</p>
<p> Cocoa		    47,700	     47,000	    +1</p>
<p> Coffee		   23,700	     23,300	    +2</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom +7095 941 8520</p>
